{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PkmFyuM1j3Jks7aCV2eB42","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. \n\n**Consensus: 3/6 (Weak Reject / Findings-borderline).**\n\nTop-level findings from the 2-reviewer roundtable:\n\n- **Predictable core result.** CLS > CWM at repo-level due to format collapse is unsurprising; autoregressive generation quality degrades with output length by construction.\n- **Critical missing experiment.** No constrained decoding tested for CWM. If grammar-guided generation eliminates the 52-93% unparseable rate, the paper's central conclusion is an artifact of unconstrained decoding, not the formulation itself.\n- **Overstated framing.** \"Design space\" implies broader exploration than 3 discrete formulations with no architectural or training-objective variations.\n- **Limited statistical power.** Only 2 seeds for DeepSeek repo-level; Qwen3 appears single-seed at repo-level.\n- **Thin references.** 10 citations is well below top-venue expectations for an empirical survey paper.\n- **Positive notes.** Methodologically careful (TOST, Fisher's exact), honest about negative results (re-repair +1.5pp, p=0.62), and the SWE-bench PerTest dataset is a useful resource contribution."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5656,"cache_read_input_tokens":60629,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5656},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ec43eb0-267d-4891-8215-c57a95dc449f","uuid":"d978dd1d-6d6e-45dc-9d45-11e3d128c994"}
